    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-055. Marks the ADR as Implemented with a **fixture-verified delta** — and records the first honest correction to a prior ADR's finding in the session.\n\n## The verified delta\n\nPermanent fixture at `docs/adr055-background-shorthand-test.html`. Screenshot 2026-11-01 confirmed:\n\n```\nRow 1 GREEN   -- longhand bg + longhand border (control)\nRow 2 BLUE    -- bg shorthand works (was WHITE pre-ADR-055)\nRow 3 ORANGE  -- border shorthand works (ADR-040, unchanged)\nRow 4 PURPLE  -- both shorthands together\nRow 5 NO FILL -- 'none' correctly overrides #c0392b (was red pre-ADR-055, text now readable)\n```\n\nAll five rows correct. **Two consecutive ADR cycles (054 + 055)** now verified via the synthetic-fixture category.\n\n## Real production delta (first since ADR-045)\n\n**7 of 11 `background:` forms now render** — `#fff`, `#ffffff`, `#fff !important`, `var(--x, #fff)`, `none`, `none !important`. These are the most common article chrome backgrounds.\n\n**4 of 11 still drop** — 3 url() forms + 1 linear-gradient. No regression: same as today.\n\n## The honest correction\n\n**ADR-054's finding was imprecise.** The original claim — \"shorthand background: and border: don't parse yet\" — was wrong. ADR-055's isolation fixture proved that **`border:` was working all along** (ADR-040's `try_expand_border` at `stylesheet.cpp:482`, tested at 889-1002).\n\nADR-054's fixture changed multiple variables at once (`box-sizing`, `margin`, `background`, `border`). The 2px border was **rendered but invisible** against white at small size, making both shorthands look broken.\n\n**Lesson recorded in ADR-054's Post-ADR-055 note**: when a fixture fails, isolate one variable per row before drawing conclusions.\n\n## What this PR carries\n\n- ADR-055 → Implemented (implementation + tests + fixture + verified screenshot)\n- **Post-ADR-055 correction note in ADR-054** (the honest record of the imprecise finding)\n- Post-ADR-055 note in ADR-040 (confirms border shorthand has been working since ADR-040; lists the `expand_shorthand` dispatcher history)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Test count\n\n- 651 → 658 cases (+7 new)\n- 2490 → 2514 assertions (+24 new)\n- Documentation only; no code changes\n\nRefs #246\n",
